    "narrative": "For June 1st, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (74.54) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.37), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez and Sandy Alcantara, respectively. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, with the algorithm factoring in a strong SP skill matchup against the left-handed Rodriguez, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a substantial platoon edge (+14%) despite a modest historical BvP struggle. **Andy Pages** (70.52) also registers as a strong start, as his neutral platoon standing against the same left-handed arm provides high-efficiency output for our lineup, solidifying the outfield and utility slots as the engine of today\u2019s projected scoring.\n\nThe lower end of our lineup highlights the specific scarcity of stolen bases in our current strategy. **Nasim Nunez** (59.34) earns a \"Strong\" designation despite a suboptimal ninth-place spot in the order. This is driven entirely by his elite speed profile and the algorithmic bump provided by his ability to exploit the slower delivery of Sandy Alcantara, which projects high stolen base efficiency. Conversely, **Miguel Vargas** (42.28) and **Sam Antonacci** (45.07) are marginal starts today; both face a formidable test in Joe Ryan (3.21 xERA). While **Sam Antonacci** shows promise with a strong xwOBA, the elite skill level of the opposing pitcher drags these projections toward the floor, necessitating caution as we manage our remaining game caps.\n\nAmong our bench, the decision-making process is largely dictated by rest, as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, our depth is intentionally constrained. Looking forward, we remain vigilant regarding the health of **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Dominic Smith**. The primary risk today involves the volatile SP skill ratings; should the weather or early-inning bullpen usage shift, we are prepared to pivot, but the current configuration maximizes our SB upside and platoon efficiency against the day's starting pitching slate.",
